From: CloudAndX <cloudandx@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] disable x86 KVM on non-x86 Linux runtimes

The x86 target configuration historically assumed that every Linux build
would run on an x86 host. Keep native Linux x86 KVM support unchanged, but
leave CONFIG_KVM unset when the x86_64 TCG guest engine is compiled for an
AArch64 runtime.

diff --git a/android-qemu2-glue/config/target-x86_64/config-target.h b/android-qemu2-glue/config/target-x86_64/config-target.h
--- a/android-qemu2-glue/config/target-x86_64/config-target.h
+++ b/android-qemu2-glue/config/target-x86_64/config-target.h
@@ -6 +6 @@
-#ifdef __linux__
+#if defined(__linux__) && (defined(__i386__) || defined(__x86_64__))
@@ -10 +10 @@
-#else // __linux__
+#else // Linux x86 host
@@ -25 +25 @@
-#endif // __linux__
+#endif // Linux x86 host
